# Readable UI (hard rule)

This is a hard stop. Grok and Composer keep shipping unreadable type. Do not.

**Never put dark text on a dark box. Never put white or light text on a white or light box.** If you cannot read the words at a glance, the screen is wrong. Stop and fix it before any other polish.

These are errors. They are not a design style. Do not ship them, do not copy them, and do not match an existing screen that has them.

## Forbidden

- Dark type (`#0a1628`, `text-slate-*`, navy) on a dark, glass, gradient, or near-black surface.
- White or light type (`text-white`, `text-white/90`, frost, `#f8fafc`) on a white, ivory, cream, or faint `bg-white/5`–`bg-white/[0.08]` surface.
- Hardcoding `text-white` on the page bed after a dark tray was removed. That is white-on-white. The tokens that were correct *inside* a dark card are wrong on ivory.
- Frosted shells (`bg-white/[0.08]`, `backdrop-blur`, `MARKETING_HUB_CONTENT_SHELL`) on a light page with white headings.
- Faded, glass, or nearly clear buttons. A control someone presses is a solid fill. The label contrasts with that fill.
- Nested trays: a box behind the boxes. Cards sit on the page bed. Do not wrap a grid of cards in another panel, room, canvas, or “screen.”
- Titles, subtitles, chips, rows, labels, placeholders, and buttons are all covered.

## Required

- Light / white / ivory surface → dark type (`#0a1628` or `text-slate-600` for secondary).
- Dark / accent / catalog card → light type (`#f8fafc` or `text-white`). Pairing is: dark card + light ink, or white card + dark ink. Never the reverse.
- Buttons are opaque. Primary is solid green with light type. Secondary is a solid fill with contrasting type, not a 5–15% white wash.
- One layer of cards on the page. If a card is the object, the page behind it is the bed, not another card.
- This applies to every admin page and every partner page, including new screens.

If a screen already has one of these, fix it. It is not a template.
